From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Martin=20=C5=A0trobl?= <recordyletsplays@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:20:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: power: reset: reboot-mode: Write the normal mode at
 boot

Samsung's S-Boot remembers the last boot mode until the reboot mode
register tells it another one. A reset that bypasses the reboot notifier
(watchdog, hang, forced reset) leaves the register alone, so after a boot
into recovery every such reset started the recovery again: a recovery
that hangs was all the phone would boot.

Write the "normal" mode when the driver registers. A reboot with a mode
still overwrites it, and a reset without one now leads to a normal boot.
---
 drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c b/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
index 485fe928e5d8..4707a22ec64e 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
@@ -119,6 +119,17 @@ int reboot_mode_register(struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot)
 		list_add_tail(&info->list, &reboot->head);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A reset that does not come through the reboot notifier (watchdog,
+	 * a hang, a forced reset) leaves the mode register as it is, and a
+	 * bootloader that remembers the last mode starts the same thing
+	 * again: a recovery that hangs is then all the phone boots. Ask for a
+	 * normal boot from the start; a reboot with a mode overwrites it.
+	 */
+	list_for_each_entry(info, &reboot->head, list)
+		if (!strcmp(info->mode, "normal"))
+			reboot->write(reboot, info->magic);
+
 	reboot->reboot_notifier.notifier_call = reboot_mode_notify;
 	register_reboot_notifier(&reboot->reboot_notifier);
 
